WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.366
<v Rohan>My weight is thirty-five kilograms!

00:00:05.366 --> 00:00:09.195
<v Mishu>Kilograms measure your mass: the amount of matter in you.

00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:12.012
<v Mishu>Weight is the pull of gravity on you.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.785
<v Ishita>So on the Moon?

00:00:13.785 --> 00:00:18.452
<v Mishu>You'd weigh about one-sixth as much, but your mass stays the same.

00:00:18.452 --> 00:00:23.618
<v Rohan>Look, the shop's balance: sugar on one pan, a kilogram weight on the other!

00:00:23.618 --> 00:00:25.798
<v Mishu>A beam balance compares masses.

00:00:25.698 --> 00:00:30.274
<v Mishu>It's true only if the pans, the arms and the strings are equal.

00:00:30.174 --> 00:00:35.336
<v Mishu>And for a hundred and thirty years, the kilogram itself was a metal block in Paris.

00:00:35.236 --> 00:00:42.424
<v Mishu>It slowly changed, so in twenty nineteen, scientists gave the kilogram a new definition that doesn't change.

00:00:42.424 --> 00:00:47.583
<v Ishita>And the goldsmith needs milligrams: a physical or an electronic balance!
